 better to keep the F2s and not discard them. So discard W5 instead.\n\nTherefore, the best move might be to discard W5. That way, they remove a tile that's not part of any potential meld and keep the F2s for possible pung. Also, discarding W5 doesn't help anyone else form a meld since they don't have W4 or W6 in the hand. So the answer would be Play W5.\n", "output": "Evaluation: [Discarding W5 is the most strategic move as it is a single tile not part of any potential meld, and keeping F2 pairs could help form a Prevalent Wind pung for 2 points.]\nReason: [W5 is a lone Character tile with no adjacent tiles in the hand, making it the least valuable. Discarding it preserves potential for honor-based scoring (F2 pairs) and avoids giving opponents a chance to form melds.]\nAnswer: Play W5"}
